{
  "markdown": "##### [cppreference.com](https://en.cppreference.com/index.html)\n\n[Create account](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Special:UserLogin&returnto=cpp%2Fstring&type=signup)\n\n- [Log in](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Special:UserLogin&returnto=cpp%2Fstring \"You are encouraged to log in; however, it is not mandatory [o]\")\n\n##### Namespaces\n\n- [Page](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/string.html \"View the content page [c]\")\n- [Discussion](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Talk:cpp/string&action=edit&redlink=1 \"Discussion about the content page [t]\")\n\n##### Variants\n\n##### Views\n\n- [View](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/string.html)\n- [Edit](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/string&action=edit \"You can edit this page. Please use the preview button before saving [e]\")\n- [History](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/string&action=history \"Past revisions of this page [h]\")\n\n##### Actions\n\n# Strings library\n\nFrom cppreference.com\n\n< [cpp](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp.html \"cpp\")\n\n[C++](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp.html \"cpp\")\n\n|     |\n| --- |\n| [Compiler support](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/compiler_support.html \"cpp/compiler support\") |\n| [Freestanding and hosted](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/freestanding.html \"cpp/freestanding\") |\n| [Language](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language.html \"cpp/language\") |\n| [Standard library](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/standard_library.html \"cpp/standard library\") |\n| [Standard library headers](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/headers.html \"cpp/header\") |\n| [Named requirements](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/iterator/concepts.html \"cpp/named req\") |\n| [Feature test macros](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/experimental/feature_test.html \"cpp/feature test\")(C++20) |\n| [Language support library](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility.html#Language_support \"cpp/utility\") |\n| [Concepts library](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/concepts.html \"cpp/concepts\")(C++20) |\n| [Diagnostics library](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/error.html \"cpp/error\") |\n| [Memory management library](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory.html \"cpp/memory\") |\n| [Metaprogramming library](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/meta.html \"cpp/meta\")(C++11) |\n| [General utilities library](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility.html \"cpp/utility\") |\n| [Containers library](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container.html \"cpp/container\") |\n| [Iterators library](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/iterator.html \"cpp/iterator\") |\n| [Ranges library](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/ranges.html \"cpp/ranges\")(C++20) |\n| [Algorithms library](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/algorithm.html \"cpp/algorithm\") |\n| **Strings library** |\n| [Text processing library](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/text.html \"cpp/text\") |\n| [Numerics library](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/numeric.html \"cpp/numeric\") |\n| [Date and time library](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/chrono.html \"cpp/chrono\") |\n| [Input/output library](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/io.html \"cpp/io\") |\n| [Filesystem library](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/filesystem.html \"cpp/filesystem\")(C++17) |\n| [Concurrency support library](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/atomic.html \"cpp/thread\")(C++11) |\n| [Execution control library](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/experimental/execution.html \"cpp/execution\")(C++26) |\n| [Technical specifications](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/experimental.html \"cpp/experimental\") |\n| [Symbols index](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/symbol_index.html \"cpp/symbol index\") |\n| [External libraries](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/links/libs.html \"cpp/links/libs\") |\n\n[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/navbar_content&action=edit)\n\n**Strings library**\n\n|     |\n| --- |\n| Classes |\n| [basic\\_string](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/string/basic_string.html \"cpp/string/basic string\") |\n| [basic\\_string\\_view](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/string/basic_string_view.html \"cpp/string/basic string view\")<br>(C++17) |\n| [char\\_traits](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/string/char_traits.html \"cpp/string/char traits\") |\n\n[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/string/navbar_content&action=edit)\n\n|     |\n| --- |\n| ## Contents<br>- [1Characters](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/string.html#Characters)<br>- [2Library components](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/string.html#Library_components)<br>  - [2.1Character traits](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/string.html#Character_traits)<br>  - [2.2String classes (std::string etc.)](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/string.html#String_classes_.28std::string_etc..29)<br>  - [2.3String view classes (std::string\\_view etc.) (since C++17)](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/string.html#String_view_classes_.28std::string_view_etc..29_.28since_C.2B.2B17.29)<br>- [3Relevant libraries](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/string.html#Relevant_libraries)<br>- [4Defect reports](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/string.html#Defect_reports)<br>- [5See also](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/string.html#See_also) |\n\n### \\[ [edit](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/string&action=edit&section=1 \"Edit section: Characters\")\\]Characters\n\nIn the C++ standard library, a _character_ is an object which, when treated sequentially, can represent text.\n\nThe term means not only objects of [character types](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/type-id.html \"cpp/language/type\"), but also any value that can be represented by a type that provides the definitions specified in the strings library and following libraries:\n\n- [localization library](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/locale.html \"cpp/locale\")\n- [input/output library](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/io.html \"cpp/io\")\n\n|     |     |\n| --- | --- |\n| - [regular expressions library](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/regex.html \"cpp/regex\") | (since C++11) |\n\nIn the strings library and regular expressions library(since C++11), a character can be of only _char-like types_, i.e. those non-array types that satisfy the requirements of\n[PODType](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/named_req/PODType.html \"cpp/named req/PODType\")(until C++20)[TrivialType](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/named_req/TrivialType.html \"cpp/named req/TrivialType\") and [StandardLayoutType](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/named_req/StandardLayoutType.html \"cpp/named req/StandardLayoutType\")(since C++20)(until C++26)[TriviallyCopyable](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/named_req/TriviallyCopyable.html \"cpp/named req/TriviallyCopyable\") and [StandardLayoutType](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/named_req/StandardLayoutType.html \"cpp/named req/StandardLayoutType\")(since C++26).\n\n|     |     |\n| --- | --- |\n| For any char-like type `T`, [std::is\\_trivially\\_default\\_constructible\\_v](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/types/is_default_constructible.html) <T> is true. | (since C++26) |\n\nTherefore, characters are also referred as _char-like objects_ in the strings library and regular expressions library(since C++11).\n\nSome standard library components accept _character container types_. They, too, are types used to represent individual characters. Such types are used for one of the template arguments of [std::char\\_traits](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/string/char_traits.html \"cpp/string/char traits\") and the class templates which use [std::char\\_traits](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/string/char_traits.html \"cpp/string/char traits\").\n\n### \\[ [edit](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/string&action=edit&section=2 \"Edit section: Library components\")\\]Library components\n\nThe C++ strings library includes the following components:\n\n#### \\[ [edit](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/string&action=edit&section=3 \"Edit section: Character traits\")\\]Character traits\n\nMany character-related class templates (such as [std::basic\\_string](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/string/basic_string.html \"cpp/string/basic string\")) need a set of related types and functions to complete the definition of their semantics. These types and functions are provided as a set of member typedef names and functions in the template parameter `Traits` used by each such template. The classes which are able to complete those semantics are [CharTraits](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/named_req/CharTraits.html \"cpp/named req/CharTraits\").\n\nThe string library provides the class template [std::char\\_traits](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/string/char_traits.html \"cpp/string/char traits\") that defines types and functions for [std::basic\\_string](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/string/basic_string.html \"cpp/string/basic string\") and [std::basic\\_string\\_view](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/string/basic_string_view.html \"cpp/string/basic string view\")(since C++17).\n\nThe following specializations are defined, all of them satisfy the [CharTraits](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/named_req/CharTraits.html \"cpp/named req/CharTraits\") requirements:\n\n|     |     |     |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Defined in header `<string>` |  |  |\n| template<>class char\\_traits<char>; |  |  |\n| template<>class char\\_traits<wchar\\_t>; |  |  |\n| template<>class char\\_traits<char8\\_t>; |  | (since C++20) |\n| template<>class char\\_traits<char16\\_t>; |  | (since C++11) |\n| template<>class char\\_traits<char32\\_t>; |  | (since C++11) |\n|  |  |  |\n\nWhen a user-defined character container type for [std::basic\\_string](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/string/basic_string.html \"cpp/string/basic string\") and [std::basic\\_string\\_view](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/string/basic_string_view.html \"cpp/string/basic string view\")(since C++17) is used, it is also necessary to provide a corresponding character trait class (which can be a specialization of [std::char\\_traits](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/string/char_traits.html \"cpp/string/char traits\")).\n\n#### \\[ [edit](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/string&action=edit&section=4 \"Edit section: String classes (std::string etc.)\")\\]String classes ([std::string](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/string/basic_string.html \"cpp/string/basic string\") etc.)\n\nThe class template [std::basic\\_string](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/string/basic_string.html \"cpp/string/basic string\") generalizes how sequences of characters are manipulated and stored. String creation, manipulation, and destruction are all handled by a convenient set of class methods and related functions.\n\nSeveral specializations of [std::basic\\_string](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/string/basic_string.html \"cpp/string/basic string\") are provided for commonly-used types:\n\n|     |     |\n| --- | --- |\n| Defined in header `<string>` |\n| Type | Definition |\n| `std::string` | [std::basic\\_string](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/string/basic_string.html) <char> |\n| `std::wstring` | [std::basic\\_string](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/string/basic_string.html) <wchar\\_t> |\n| `std::u8string`(since C++20) | [std::basic\\_string](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/string/basic_string.html) <char8\\_t> |\n| `std::u16string`(since C++11) | [std::basic\\_string](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/string/basic_string.html) <char16\\_t> |\n| `std::u32string`(since C++11) | [std::basic\\_string](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/string/basic_string.html) <char32\\_t> |\n\n#### \\[ [edit](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/string&action=edit&section=5 \"Edit section: String view classes (std::string view etc.) (since C++17)\")\\]String view classes ([std::string\\_view](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/string/basic_string_view.html \"cpp/string/basic string view\") etc.) (since C++17)\n\nThe class template [std::basic\\_string\\_view](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/string/basic_string_view.html \"cpp/string/basic string view\") provides a lightweight object that offers read-only access to a string or a part of a string using an interface similar to the interface of [std::basic\\_string](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/string/basic_string.html \"cpp/string/basic string\").\n\nSeveral specializations of [std::basic\\_string\\_view](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/string/basic_string_view.html \"cpp/string/basic string view\") are provided for commonly-used types:\n\n|     |     |\n| --- | --- |\n| Defined in header `<string_view>` |\n| Type | Definition |\n| `std::string_view` | [std::basic\\_string\\_view](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/string/basic_string_view.html) <char> |\n| `std::wstring_view` | [std::basic\\_string\\_view](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/string/basic_string_view.html) <wchar\\_t> |\n| `std::u8string_view`(since C++20) | [std::basic\\_string\\_view](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/string/basic_string_view.html) <char8\\_t> |\n| `std::u16string_view` | [std::basic\\_string\\_view](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/string/basic_string_view.html) <char16\\_t> |\n| `std::u32string_view` | [std::basic\\_string\\_view](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/string/basic_string_view.html) <char32\\_t> |\n\n### \\[ [edit](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/string&action=edit&section=6 \"Edit section: Relevant libraries\")\\]Relevant libraries\n\nThe [text processing library](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/text.html \"cpp/text\") provides support for localizations, string conversions (e.g. [`std::toupper`](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/locale/toupper.html \"cpp/locale/toupper\")), character classification functions (e.g. [`std::isspace`](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/locale/isspace.html \"cpp/locale/isspace\")), and text encoding recognition ( [`std::text_encoding`](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/locale/text_encoding.html \"cpp/text/text encoding\")).\n\n### \\[ [edit](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/string&action=edit&section=7 \"Edit section: Defect reports\")\\]Defect reports\n\nThe following behavior-changing defect reports were applied retroactively to previously published C++ standards.\n\n| DR | Applied to | Behavior as published | Correct behavior |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| [LWG 1170](https://cplusplus.github.io/LWG/issue1170) | C++98 | char-like types could be array types | prohibited |\n\n### \\[ [edit](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/string&action=edit&section=8 \"Edit section: See also\")\\]See also\n\n|     |\n| --- |\n| [C documentation](https://en.cppreference.com/w/c/string.html \"c/string\") for Strings library |\n\nRetrieved from \" [https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/string&oldid=179902](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/string&oldid=179902)\"\n\n##### Navigation\n\n- [Support us](http://www.cppreference.com/support)\n- [Recent changes](https://en.cppreference.com/w/Special:RecentChanges \"A list of recent changes in the wiki [r]\")\n- [FAQ](https://en.cppreference.com/w/Cppreference%253AAbout.html)\n- [Offline version](https://en.cppreference.com/w/Cppreference%253AArchives.html)\n\n##### Toolbox\n\n- [What links here](https://en.cppreference.com/w/Special:WhatLinksHere/cpp/string \"A list of all wiki pages that link here [j]\")\n- [Related changes](https://en.cppreference.com/w/Special:RecentChangesLinked/cpp/string \"Recent changes in pages linked from this page [k]\")\n- [Upload file](http://upload.cppreference.com/w/Special:Upload \"Upload files [u]\")\n- [Special pages](https://en.cppreference.com/w/Special:SpecialPages \"A list of all special pages [q]\")\n- [Printable version](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/string&printable=yes \"Printable version of this page [p]\")\n- [Permanent link](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/string&oldid=179902 \"Permanent link to this revision of the page\")\n- [Page information](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/string&action=info)\n\n- In other languages\n\n- [\u0627\u0644\u0639\u0631\u0628\u064a\u0629](http://ar.cppreference.com/w/cpp/string \"cpp/string\")\n- [Deutsch](http://de.cppreference.com/w/cpp/string \"cpp/string\")\n- [Espa\u00f1ol](http://es.cppreference.com/w/cpp/string \"cpp/string\")\n- [Fran\u00e7ais](http://fr.cppreference.com/w/cpp/string \"cpp/string\")\n- [Italiano](http://it.cppreference.com/w/cpp/string \"cpp/string\")\n- [\u65e5\u672c\u8a9e](http://ja.cppreference.com/w/cpp/string \"cpp/string\")\n- [Portugu\u00eas](http://pt.cppreference.com/w/cpp/string \"cpp/string\")\n- [\u0420\u0443\u0441\u0441\u043a\u0438\u0439](http://ru.cppreference.com/w/cpp/string \"cpp/string\")\n- [\u4e2d\u6587](http://zh.cppreference.com/w/cpp/string \"cpp/string\")\n\n- This page was last modified on 28 January 2025, at 12:14.\n\n- [Privacy policy](https://en.cppreference.com/w/Cppreference%253APrivacy_policy.html \"Cppreference:Privacy policy\")\n- [About cppreference.com](https://en.cppreference.com/w/Cppreference%253AAbout.html \"Cppreference:About\")\n- [Disclaimers](https://en.cppreference.com/w/Cppreference%253AGeneral_disclaimer.html \"Cppreference:General disclaimer\")\n\n- [![Powered by MediaWiki](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/skins/common/images/poweredby_mediawiki_88x31.png)](https://www.mediawiki.org/)[![Powered by GeSHi](https://upload.cppreference.com/mwiki/images/2/2b/powered_by_geshi_88x31.png)](http://qbnz.com/highlighter/)[![Hosted by Tiger Technologies](https://upload.cppreference.com/mwiki/images/9/94/powered_by_tigertech_88x31.png)](http://www.tigertech.net/referral/cppreference.com)",
